[1m[38;5;231mWhich approach for the shared validation layer?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mRule table (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mvalidate(values, rules) + validator primitives. New form = a rule object + one call. ~25 lines, no DOM coupling. [39m
     [38;5;246mCan grow a binding layer later.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Rule table + DOM binding
     [38;5;246mAdds auto-reading values from the form element and rendering errors. Least per-form code, but invents markup [39m
     [38;5;246mconventions for forms that don't exist.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Primitives only
     [38;5;246mShare just required() etc.; each form writes its own validate function. Minimal abstraction, but each form repeats
[39m     [38;5;246mthe collect logic.[39m
